  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"El presente libro es una especie de cuaderno preparatorio para el proyecto de la ópera rock El gallo de oro. Como tal, reúne información de modo más o meno pertidente, desordenado y aleatorio, para tratar de formar e ilustrar la idea de la pieza y definir su naturaleza."--Page 12. "The Golden Cockerel ... is an opera in three acts (with a short prologue and an even shorter epilogue) by Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov. The libretto was written by Vladimir Belsky and is based on Alexander Pushkin's 1834 poem The Tale of the Golden Cockerel (which is based on two chapters of Tales of the Alhambra by Washington Irving). The opera was completed in 1907, but did not receive its premiere in Moscow until 1909, after the composer's death. Previously, the opera was commonly performed in French under the still recognized title Le Coq d'Or."--Page 17.</subfield>
